{"availability":"available","full":"yidans/forge-demo","name":"forge-demo","description":"FORGE: LLM-assisted ERGM specification and interpretation under statistical checks (AAAI-27 demo). Live demo + runnable local system.","category":"AI & machine learning","language":"R","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-07-08T21:16:38Z","updated":"2026-09-19T00:08:56Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://yidans.github.io/forge-demo/","topics":["demo","ergm","llm","network-science","r","social-networks","statnet"],"demo":"https://yidans.github.io/forge-demo/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T13:01:08.575Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-08T13:01:08.575Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-08T13:01:08.575Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-08T13:01:08.575Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["FORGE is a runnable local system for guarded LLM-assisted Exponential Random Graph Model (ERGM) specification and interpretation. Given a binary network and a short domain description, it builds a graph-specific menu of valid ERGM terms, asks an LLM for structured candidate formulas, fits and compares those candidates using simulation-based goodness of fit, allows up to four rounds of checked revision, and produces a non-causal, model-grounded explanation.","Paper: FORGE: An LLM-Assisted System for Proposing and Testing Explanations of Network Tie Formation (AAAI-27 Demonstrations track submission).","The repository contains the complete local workflow:"],"features":["Network intake — validate the network and compute diagnostics.","Valid-term construction — build the ERGM terms supported by the graph","LLM proposal — request JSON candidate formulas using only valid terms.","Fitting and selection — apply formula guardrails, fit each candidate","Checked revision — for up to four rounds, feed the current model, its"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/yidans/forge-demo/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"bd564a76c2